    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_7ee0c9381f36241c008d6abe6a1ff64d299745fcdc565487d011ff5b0763f0a2",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The source separates a weak pair-correlation statement proved conditionally on RH and further assumptions, the broader pair-correlation/GUE expectation, and extensive numerical agreement. None of these supplies the missing self-adjoint operator required by Hilbert-Polya. As a speculative alternative, the author suggests that Fourier truncation and convolution phenomena may account for the sine-kernel-shaped statistic without a literal spectral realization.",
