    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_f7396de37e1f7701ba8ddab88b83c593a1e3fd62abd414fcdb6a694f4f5f7c9e",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "A formal termwise comparison maps prime logarithms to primitive-orbit periods and suggests zero Maslov phase and specified instability data for a hypothetical Polya system. The opposite sign of the oscillatory contribution is an obstruction to this naive match, not a proof that every quantum-chaos realization is impossible. The author instead favors the interpretation that arithmetic and dynamical zeta functions share trace-formula formalism, with Poisson-Newton proposed as a common source.",
