    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_433e9f534c04353da5697b89b4fb896626dbd06bbb3fe56a9164b9d170cab0e0",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A concrete representation chain runs through the source: logarithmic differentiation turns multiplicative Euler and Hadamard factorizations into additive prime and zero data; Mellin or Fourier inversion turns that data into explicit formulas; test functions and Poisson-Newton reorganize it as distributional or trace identities; adelic local Fourier-Mellin transforms instead assemble the finite and archimedean factors and their functional equation.",
