    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8753f2e3b3f3ba3e7952dd195f310e691cb77eb27b29d0ebe27d89faaefd0756",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The parent units connect the forecast ingredients through a specific transfer problem: family algebra can define exact local composition rules, but its primewise extension lacks a well-defined discrete global divisor; a usable global Euler proxy must therefore preserve arithmetic frequency data through analytic continuation, Fourier-complex analysis must mediate the local-global representations, and only then could a positivity pairing convert the assembled structure into a zero-location constraint.",
