    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_d0c77163dd7dd74afdd3da414cb920b4a8b30f2ed5c04f0f2b623311212f134a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Finite-field cohomology converts local point counts into finite-dimensional Frobenius factors whose rationality, duality, degrees, and critical absolute values can be handled separately, but multiplying such factors over primes replaces one periodic rational problem by a transcendental product at incommensurable frequencies. Automorphic representation theory can parameterize the local factors and their expected duality without itself supplying the required global analytic continuation.",
